# ONNX Runtime for this platform, which the person cutout loads at run time,
# is build input, fetched rather than committed:
#
#   bash dev/fetch-models.sh --models tauri-app/models --runtime tauri-app/onnxruntime
#
# tauri.conf.json lists onnxruntime/ under bundle.resources, and `cargo tauri
# build` refuses a resource folder that is not there, so this file keeps the
# folder in the tree. With nothing in it the app builds and has no cutout,
# which is how a CI build and a developer build work.
/*
!.gitignore
